CPS-2 WIDE release build: do not link SDL2_image

WHY. FBNeo's SDL2 build links SDL2_image for ONE call — an optional per-game
preview PNG in its own game-browser GUI (`LoadTitleImage`, support/titles/<name>.png).
That single call drags in the whole Homebrew image-codec chain: measured on
macos-arm64, the release bundle is 24 files, of which 21 are transitive codecs
(AVIF, JPEG-XL, TIFF, WebP, brotli, dav1d, lcms2, zstd...). Nothing in this project
uses any of them: the launcher starts the emulator directly with the set, and no
title set is shipped, so the NULL path this patch makes unconditional is the path
that already ran.

WHAT IT BUYS (GitHub #144). macOS refuses to run an ad-hoc-signed download and the
no-terminal remedy — System Settings > Privacy & Security > "Open Anyway" — must be
done PER BLOCKED FILE. MEASURED: the maintainer's MAME bundle is 2 files and cost 2
approvals. COUNTED, not exercised: the FBNeo bundle was 24 files and is 4 with this
patch. The step from files to approvals assumes ONE approval per blocked file — it fits
the single MAME data point and nobody has yet approved a 24- or 4-file bundle, so treat
4 as the expected cost, not a measured one. Notarization would remove
the question entirely and is not being bought.

SCOPE. Frontend only, like the harness patch 0001, and NOT emulation: the makefile's
link flag, one call site in `src/burner/sdl/sdl2_gui.cpp`, and an unused include in
`src/intf/video/sdl/vid_sdl2.cpp` (unused, but it makes the sdl2_image HEADERS a build
prerequisite, so it goes too). No CPU, sprite, timing or QSound code is touched.

COST. FBNeo's own game-browser GUI no longer shows per-game preview images. It only
ever showed them for someone who had installed a support/titles/ image set, which no
release here ships.

---
diff --git a/makefile.sdl2 b/makefile.sdl2
index 3bf65bd..ad4437a 100644
--- a/makefile.sdl2
+++ b/makefile.sdl2
@@ -96,11 +96,11 @@ incdir	= $(foreach dir,$(alldir),-I$(srcdir)$(dir)) -I$(objdir)dep/generated \
 		  -I$(srcdir)intf/input/sdl `sdl2-config --cflags`
 
 ifdef WINDOWS
-lib	= -lstdc++ `sdl2-config --libs` -lopengl32 -lSDL2_image -lm
+lib	= -lstdc++ `sdl2-config --libs` -lopengl32 -lm
 else ifdef DARWIN
-lib	= -lstdc++ `sdl2-config --libs` -lSDL2_image -lm -lpthread
+lib	= -lstdc++ `sdl2-config --libs` -lm -lpthread
 else
-lib	= -lstdc++ `sdl2-config --libs` -lGL -lSDL2_image -lm -lpthread
+lib	= -lstdc++ `sdl2-config --libs` -lGL -lm -lpthread
 endif
 
 ifdef FORCE_PULSE_AUDIO
diff --git a/src/burner/sdl/sdl2_gui.cpp b/src/burner/sdl/sdl2_gui.cpp
index 1ec99d7..371219b 100644
--- a/src/burner/sdl/sdl2_gui.cpp
+++ b/src/burner/sdl/sdl2_gui.cpp
@@ -1,4 +1,3 @@
-#include <SDL_image.h>
 #include "burner.h"
 #include "sdl2_gui_common.h"
 #include "misc_image.h"
@@ -60,7 +59,14 @@ SDL_Texture* LoadTitleImage(SDL_Renderer* renderer, SDL_Texture* loadedTexture)
 #else
 	snprintf(titlePath, MAX_PATH, "support\\titles\\%s.png", BurnDrvGetTextA(0));
 #endif
-	loadedTexture = IMG_LoadTexture(renderer, titlePath);
+	// CPS-2 WIDE release build: SDL2_image is not linked, so the optional per-game
+	// preview PNG is not loaded. This is the path that already ran whenever
+	// support/titles/<game>.png was absent, which is the normal case for a release
+	// that ships no title set. Dropping the library removes 21 transitive image
+	// codecs from the bundle (24 files -> 4), which on macOS is 24 Gatekeeper
+	// approvals -> 4 for a player who uses the System Settings route (GitHub #144).
+	(void)titlePath;
+	loadedTexture = NULL;
 	SDL_QueryTexture(loadedTexture, NULL, NULL, &w, &h);
 
 	title_texture_rect.x = 0; //the x coordinate
diff --git a/src/intf/video/sdl/vid_sdl2.cpp b/src/intf/video/sdl/vid_sdl2.cpp
index 80cab01..0eaa0e0 100644
--- a/src/intf/video/sdl/vid_sdl2.cpp
+++ b/src/intf/video/sdl/vid_sdl2.cpp
@@ -8,7 +8,6 @@
 #endif
 
 #include <SDL.h>
-#include <SDL_image.h>
 
 extern int vsync;
 extern char videofiltering[3];
